00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:55.730
All right, so almost all
of you chose radiation,

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:58.180
so, exactly, that's kind of
one of the strongest sources

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:00.510
of mutations.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:01.970
So, basically, radiation,

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:04.250
what it does is that
it's super high energy,

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:07.580
and it just hits your DNA and
like breaks it pretty much.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:11.410
So your cells try to put
together your DNA to fix it,

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:13.350
but sometimes it makes mistakes.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:14.183
And that way,

00:09:14.183 --> 00:09:17.610
you can get mutations
that could hit an oncogene

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:18.763
or a tumor suppressor.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.260
Infections, some of you
also voted for that.

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:23.950
And that's also correct.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.360
So there are certain viruses
and certain bacteria that,

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:28.670
when they're left untreated,

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:32.110
can lead to cancer by
causing, again, mutations.

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:34.320
So one example is HPV,

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.660
which causes cervical cancer.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.490
So that's why we have this HPV vaccine now

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:42.130
that they call a cancer
prevention vaccine,

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:45.530
because it really does do
that by preventing HPV.

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:47.360
Another example of a bacteria

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:49.590
that could do this is called H. pylori.

00:09:49.590 --> 00:09:53.500
So it's bacteria that infects your stomach

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:54.580
and causes ulcers.

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:57.050
And then over time, as
that infection continues,

00:09:57.050 --> 00:10:00.173
you can develop gastric
cancer, stomach cancer.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:03.560
A lot of you guys chose
